1
00:02:46,770 --> 00:02:49,410
Yes, ma'am,
how ya doin'?

2
00:02:49,470 --> 00:02:51,780
Is this Rose Hill?

3
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:54,410
Good,
This is Ed Couch.

4
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,930
I'm Vesta Adcock's nephew.

5
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:59,220
I need to get up there
and see her,

6
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:03,290
but I'm gonna be late
'cause I'm lost out here.

7
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:05,830
We're off the Alabama interstate
but I don't know where.

8
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:46,170
- Did you hear that?
- What?

9
00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:48,300
The train.

10
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:51,240
No, I didn't hear
no train.

11
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,340
Oh, nothin',
I guess.

12
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:59,820
- Where's "Whistle Stop"
on the map?
- I can't find it.

13
00:03:59,870 --> 00:04:03,750
Why did you tell me to
turn right 10 miles back there?

14
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:08,820
God, you got a negative
sense of direction, hon.

15
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:11,760
I'm sorry.

16
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:16,030
Oh, Ed,your aunt's gonna be
so disappointed we're late.

17
00:04:16,090 --> 00:04:20,100
I know she's
been looking forward to
this visit all week long.

18
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:23,440
Bless her sweet,
little ol' heart.

19
00:04:27,570 --> 00:04:30,450
Hey, how's my sweet Auntie V
this afternoon?

20
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:33,110
Remember us?

21
00:04:33,170 --> 00:04:36,240
- Don't you look pretty!
- We brought you something.

22
00:04:36,310 --> 00:04:39,480
- Let me look at you.

23
00:04:39,550 --> 00:04:42,160
Don't you know
Evelyn loves you?

24
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:47,070
Well, honey,
I guess it'd be better if
you wait out here for me.

25
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:51,590
-I'll get all this stuff.
- Well, if you think it's best.

26
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:54,970
Yeah, I do this time.
Okay?

27
00:04:55,030 --> 00:04:57,200
Have a nice day,
Aunt Vesta.

28
00:04:57,270 --> 00:04:59,220
Don't you pitch a fit
like that'

29
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:13,890
Did you know
they took my gallbladder out?

30
00:05:15,320 --> 00:05:17,460
No, I didn't.

31
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:21,200
Oh, yes. Still
in the hospital in ajar.

32
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:26,070
I guess that's where
they keep 'em.

33
00:05:26,130 --> 00:05:28,110
I guess.

34
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:30,400
When I was
in the hospital,

35
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:34,430
the nurse gave me one of them
Fleet enemas they're so fond of.

36
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:37,110
Mrs. Cleo Threadgoode,

37
00:05:37,170 --> 00:05:40,480
82 year old widow,
imagine that.

38
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:43,680
Actually,
everybody calls me Ninny.

39
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:45,980
'Course I'm
just visitin' here.

40
00:05:46,050 --> 00:05:51,330
Did you ever have
one of them Fleet enemas?

41
00:05:51,390 --> 00:05:53,340
Um,well?

42
00:05:53,390 --> 00:05:55,460
No.

43
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:58,760
You'd remember it.

44
00:05:58,830 --> 00:06:02,510
Me and my friend, Mrs. Otis,
come from Whistle Stop.

45
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:04,770
You ever been
to Whistle Stop?

46
00:06:04,830 --> 00:06:08,240
Why, yes. I just
passed by there today.

47
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:13,180
She's lived
down the street from me
for 30 years or more.

48
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:15,240
After her son died,

49
00:06:15,310 --> 00:06:18,920
her daughter-in-law had a fit
for her to come live
at the nursing home.

50
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:22,290
They asked me to come
and be her roommate.

51
00:06:22,350 --> 00:06:26,590
Mrs. Otis don't know it,
but I'm going home just soon
as she gets settled in good.

52
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:32,330
Does the name
"Idgie Threadgoode"
ring a bell?

53
00:06:32,390 --> 00:06:35,930
Um, no, ma'am.
I don't think so.

54
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,810
You'd remember her.

55
00:06:38,870 --> 00:06:42,780
You see,
I was practically adopted
by the Threadgoode family.

56
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:45,180
- I married her brother, Cleo.
- Oh, uh-huh.

57
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:52,860
Oh, now, let's see.

58
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:56,390
I 'member the day they pulled
that truck up out of the river.

59
00:07:03,780 --> 00:07:07,560
I 'member the day we
was all gettin' ready
for Leona's weddin'.

60
00:07:07,620 --> 00:07:09,600
The war had just ended,

61
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:12,000
the Great one,
you know.

62
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:16,740
And another one
was about to begin in
the Threadgoode house.

63
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:19,250
Sipsey hone )4
is that finished?

64
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:23,750
- Buddy,
get dressed honey.
- Mama?

65
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:25,780
Leona, what is it?

66
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:27,720
Idgie's upstairs
in her room...

67
00:07:27,770 --> 00:07:29,750
and says she won't come out
as long as she lives.

68
00:07:29,810 --> 00:07:31,950
- She is gonna ruin my weddin'!
- Shh.

69
00:07:32,010 --> 00:07:34,820
Leona, you're gonna be
the most beautiful bride.

70
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:38,160
Of course she is, Papa.

71
00:07:38,220 --> 00:07:42,170
Your papa has spent
every last nickel he has
just to make you happy.

72
00:07:42,220 --> 00:07:46,030
Now, you try to act
a little grateful, young lady.

73
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:49,200
Imogene Louise Threadgoode!

74
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:51,800
This is your mama!

75
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:59,150
You come down here right now.
Do you hear me?

76
00:07:59,210 --> 00:08:01,850
- Buddy, fetch her.
She'll listen to you.
- Come on down, little bit.

77
00:08:01,910 --> 00:08:04,480
There's no firin'
squad waitin' for you.

78
00:08:04,540 --> 00:08:09,890
Ohh! Come on, honey
Let us see you.

79
00:08:09,950 --> 00:08:12,120
You look so pretty.

80
00:08:12,190 --> 00:08:15,030
- I see London,
I see-
- Hush!

81
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:20,210
Julian, hush.

82
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:23,000
Come ahead, sweetheart.

83
00:08:23,060 --> 00:08:26,800
You look awful nice
in that.

84
00:08:26,870 --> 00:08:28,470
- Mama!
- You look fine.

85
00:08:28,530 --> 00:08:31,030
She looks like a monkey

86
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:32,910
Julian, stop it
right this second!

87
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:36,320
Take it back!
Take it back!
Idgie, hey!

88
00:08:36,380 --> 00:08:39,490
I told you she
was gonna ruin my weddin'!

89
00:08:39,550 --> 00:08:41,930
- Idgie, get up.
- Take it back!

90
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:44,150
Take it back!

91
00:08:44,220 --> 00:08:47,570
- I'll get you for this.
- No, Buddy.

92
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:54,430
We have to be careful
when she's dressing up.

93
00:08:54,490 --> 00:08:56,440
She's just a pain!

94
00:08:56,500 --> 00:09:00,040
Leona, will you
stop shrieking'

95
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:02,810
This is your
weddin ' day'

96
00:09:13,810 --> 00:09:16,650
I oaks like you got yourself
up a tree, little bit.

97
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:19,760
I'm sick of people
makin' fun of me.

98
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:22,360
So you're gonna stay up here
all day long.

99
00:09:22,420 --> 00:09:25,630
Yep.
The hell with them.

100
00:09:25,690 --> 00:09:29,640
Who wants to wear
that stupid ol' dress anyway?

101
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:33,080
- I ever tell you about the oysters?
- Oysters?

102
00:09:33,130 --> 00:09:35,080
- I tell you about the oysters?
- No.

103
00:09:35,130 --> 00:09:39,810
Think about the millions of
oysters lyin' around the ocean.

104
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:42,210
Then one day...

105
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:45,090
God comes along and sees one
and he says,

106
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:48,050
"I think I'm gonna make
that one different."

107
00:09:48,110 --> 00:09:50,320
You know what he does?

108
00:09:50,380 --> 00:09:53,550
He puts a little
piece of sand in it.

109
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:57,860
- Guess what it can do
that the others can't.
- What?

110
00:09:57,920 --> 00:10:01,230
It can make
a beautiful pearl.

111
00:10:01,290 --> 00:10:03,460
What if God
made a mistake?

112
00:10:03,530 --> 00:10:08,640
Well, the way I figure it,
he never makes mistakes.

113
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:11,480
I mean, he made sure
we got together.

114
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:13,540
He made sure you got
the best looking,

115
00:10:13,610 --> 00:10:15,820
most charmin' brother
in the world...

116
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:19,260
- who's gonna beat you
to the chocolate cake.
- You will not.

117
00:10:19,310 --> 00:10:21,690
Got you out of the tree,
didn't I?

118
00:10:21,750 --> 00:10:24,700
Did not!

119
00:10:24,750 --> 00:10:28,390
Into this estate,
these two come now to be joined

120
00:10:28,450 --> 00:10:30,560
If any man present
can show cause...

121
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:33,030
why they may not lawfully
be joined together,

122
00:10:33,090 --> 00:10:38,230
let him speak now or
forever after hold his peace.

123
00:10:38,300 --> 00:10:40,970
Please be seated.

124
00:10:43,340 --> 00:10:45,550
If either of you
know any reason...

125
00:10:45,610 --> 00:10:48,590
why you may not justly
be joined together
in holy matrimony

126
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:51,120
do you now confess it?

127
00:11:00,750 --> 00:11:03,460
It is then your will
to proceed.

128
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:07,230
Do you,
Charles Osgood justice-

129
00:11:13,070 --> 00:11:16,420
Thank you. I don't know what
we'd do without your generosity.

130
00:11:16,470 --> 00:11:19,450
Sipsey, especially you.
Look what you've clone!

131
00:11:19,510 --> 00:11:23,460
Thank you, Mrs. Threadgoode.
Gimme that, you rascal!

132
00:11:27,780 --> 00:11:30,350
John!
Jump on my back

133
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:34,060
I don't think
there ever was a sweeter boy
than Buddy Threadgoode.

134
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:38,630
- You look beautiful, Lily.
- Yes, Lily, you sure do.

135
00:11:38,690 --> 00:11:42,140
I had the biggest crush
on him.

136
00:11:42,190 --> 00:11:44,530
He was a terrible flirt!

137
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:47,840
But his heart belonged
to Ruth Jamison.

138
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:51,070
She was the daughter of
a friend of his mama's...

139
00:11:51,140 --> 00:11:53,950
who was visitin'
that summer.

140
00:11:54,010 --> 00:11:57,480
Ruth Jamison,
you're just the one
I've been lookin' for.

141
00:11:57,540 --> 00:12:00,650
- Are you thirsty?
- Let's go visit
someplace else.

142
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:09,900
Think that's a big lake,
you should've seen the
one next to our house.

143
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:12,100
We used to swim in it
and fish.

144
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:14,830
I sure do miss it.
Sure do.

145
00:12:14,890 --> 00:12:17,630
What happened to it?
Did it dry up?

146
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:19,650
No, worse than that.

147
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:21,770
Last fall,
a ﬂock of ducks,

148
00:12:21,830 --> 00:12:26,110
40 or 50 of 'em,
landed right smack
in the middle of it.

149
00:12:26,170 --> 00:12:28,050
This ﬂuke thing
happened.

150
00:12:28,110 --> 00:12:30,590
The temperature dropped so fast
that the whole lake froze...

151
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:32,640
in three seconds,
just like that!

152
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:35,020
Those poor little ducks.
Did it kill them?

153
00:12:35,080 --> 00:12:38,290
No, they ﬂew off
and took the lake with 'em.

154
00:12:38,350 --> 00:12:41,730
To this very day, that lake
is somewhere over in Georgia.

155
00:12:41,790 --> 00:12:45,240
Buddy Threadgoode.

156
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:59,550
Come a little closer.
I wanna give you something.

157
00:12:59,610 --> 00:13:02,060
Come here.

158
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:08,150
Whoop!

159
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:15,690
Come back here, hat. Where
do you think you're gain'?

160
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:19,870
Whoa!

161
00:13:19,930 --> 00:13:23,040
I got it.
Hold on, Ruth.
Hold on, little bit.

162
00:13:27,430 --> 00:13:30,170
It's all right.
I got it.

163
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:36,040
Come here,
you damn hat.
Got it!

164
00:13:36,110 --> 00:13:39,060
Oh, I meant
to do that.

165
00:13:40,110 --> 00:13:43,850
I... got it!

166
00:13:43,920 --> 00:13:45,800
Ta-da!

167
00:13:47,590 --> 00:13:50,130
All right.
Damn!

168
00:13:50,190 --> 00:13:52,170
Come on.

169
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:03,680
Come on. Get out.
Get out.

170
00:14:03,740 --> 00:14:05,690
Buddy!

171
00:14:05,740 --> 00:14:08,980
- Buddy!
- Buddy Threadgoode!

172
00:14:10,610 --> 00:14:12,320
Come on, Buddy!

173
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:14,120
Get out.

174
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:17,720
Get out of there.

175
00:14:19,050 --> 00:14:22,860
Buddy!

176
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:26,060
- Come on, Buddy!
- Buddy'

177
00:14:26,130 --> 00:14:28,740
Buddy!

178
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:33,870
No-o-o!

179
00:14:33,930 --> 00:14:37,780
Buddy!

180
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:41,250
Buddy, no!
No!

181
00:14:41,310 --> 00:14:44,090
No! Buddy!
No-o-o!

182
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:47,180
No! Buddy!
Let me go!

183
00:14:48,650 --> 00:14:52,460
' No!
- Buddy!

184
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:56,160
- You got to go back to the house.

185
00:14:56,220 --> 00:14:58,720
Come on.
We're gonna go home.

186
00:14:58,790 --> 00:15:01,630
- Buddy!
- You have to be strong.

187
00:15:01,690 --> 00:15:04,600
- It'll be okay.
- Buddy!

188
00:15:04,660 --> 00:15:07,610
"The Lord is my Shepherd,

189
00:15:07,670 --> 00:15:09,880
I shall not want."

190
00:15:09,940 --> 00:15:12,940
Oh, it like
to have killed us all

191
00:15:13,010 --> 00:15:15,680
But nary a one took it
as hard as Idgie,

192
00:15:18,780 --> 00:15:24,250
everyone thought she 'o' die
right along with him.

193
00:15:40,900 --> 00:15:45,180
Night alter night,
she stayed by the river.

194
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:49,420
Big George was the only soul
she'd let near her,

195
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:53,020
and he watched over her
night and day

196
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:55,890
You know,
a heart can be broken,

197
00:15:55,950 --> 00:15:59,020
but it still keeps a-beatin'
just the same.

198
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:01,720
Miss Idgie, you'll have
to keep this blanket on...

199
00:16:01,790 --> 00:16:04,700
or you'll catch
your death of cold,
you hear me now?

200
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:09,180
That's so sad.

201
00:16:14,570 --> 00:16:17,180
Ah.

202
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:19,240
Would you like
one of these?

203
00:16:19,310 --> 00:16:21,310
Oh, thank ya,
honey.

204
00:16:21,370 --> 00:16:23,250
Evelyn?

205
00:16:23,310 --> 00:16:25,480
Honey,
we gotta get goin'.

206
00:16:25,540 --> 00:16:27,950
The Braves' game's
fixin' to start...

207
00:16:28,010 --> 00:16:29,650
and you're gonna miss
your... thing.

208
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:33,460
Excuse me.
That's my husband, Ed.

209
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:35,590
Hi, ma'am.
How you doin'?

210
00:16:35,650 --> 00:16:39,100
Um.

211
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:41,230
I can't believe
Buddy died.

212
00:16:41,290 --> 00:16:43,900
Neither could I.

213
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:47,370
Oh, well, I enjoyed
talkin' to you, honey.

214
00:16:47,430 --> 00:16:49,430
What's your name?

215
00:16:49,500 --> 00:16:52,570
Evelyn...
Evelyn Couch.

216
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:57,420
- I've got to go.
- You come back and see me,
you hear?

217
00:16:57,480 --> 00:17:01,390
- Okay.
- Bye-bye.

218
00:17:01,580 --> 00:17:03,860
First of all,
I want you...

219
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:06,530
to truly
dedicate yourselves...

220
00:17:06,590 --> 00:17:10,630
to finding little ways
to putting that magic,
that spark...

221
00:17:10,690 --> 00:17:12,900
back into your marriage.

222
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:16,910
When we think of
romance and marriage,

223
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:21,000
- what is the first thought
that comes into your mind?
- Divorce!

224
00:17:21,070 --> 00:17:24,780
Remember when counselors
used to tell you to wrap
yourself in cellophane...

225
00:17:24,840 --> 00:17:27,050
to put a little charge
into your marriage?

226
00:17:27,110 --> 00:17:29,920
Do we really pay
for these lectures?

227
00:17:29,980 --> 00:17:32,690
You can see,
it is truly up to you...

228
00:17:32,750 --> 00:17:36,250
to put romance back
into your relationship.

229
00:18:03,940 --> 00:18:05,920
Evelyn,
have you gone insane?

230
00:18:05,980 --> 00:18:07,930
My God
people can see you!

231
00:18:07,980 --> 00:18:10,050
What if I had been
the paperboy?

232
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:11,900
Get in there!

233
00:18:11,950 --> 00:18:14,760
What are you
thinking about?

234
00:18:15,550 --> 00:18:18,900
Evelyn?

235
00:18:18,960 --> 00:18:21,270
- Evelyn!
- Oh.

236
00:18:21,330 --> 00:18:25,300
You know, what we really need
instead of this baloney...

237
00:18:25,360 --> 00:18:29,430
is an assertiveness
training class for
Southern women.

238
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:33,070
But that's a contradiction
in terms, isn't it?

239
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:36,380
Especially you, sweetheart.
You're livin' in the Dark Ages.

240
00:18:59,630 --> 00:19:02,240
- Hi, honey.
I need one of those.
- Hi!

241
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:05,080
Mmm, you smell good too.

242
00:19:05,140 --> 00:19:07,180
I need one of these.

243
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:10,190
- Oh, this looks good!
- Uh-huh.

244
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:12,190
Yes, indeedy.

245
00:19:21,350 --> 00:19:24,330
Ed.

246
00:19:26,020 --> 00:19:28,190
Why don't you come in?
and sit down at the table...

247
00:19:28,260 --> 00:19:32,210
- and have dinner with me?
- I'm sorry.
The game's almost over.

248
00:19:32,260 --> 00:19:35,100
I just want to see
a little bit of it.
Why you so dressed up?

249
00:19:35,170 --> 00:19:37,670
Honey, don't get in the way.
Scoot over a bit.

250
00:19:41,810 --> 00:19:43,380
Ed?

251
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:46,440
If I'd answered the door
wearing only cellophane,

252
00:19:46,510 --> 00:19:49,820
would you still be
watching the baseball game?

253
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:53,620
No, honey. I'd probably
be checking you into
a looney bin.

254
00:20:15,940 --> 00:20:20,180
Hi, sugar.

255
00:20:20,250 --> 00:20:22,200
- How's my dumplin'?
- Trick or treat!

256
00:20:22,250 --> 00:20:24,200
You 're not gonna throw
them hissy-fits, are you?

257
00:20:24,250 --> 00:20:27,490
Happy Halloween!
Oh, no. No, no, no!

258
00:20:27,550 --> 00:20:29,660
You 're meaner
than a damn snake.

259
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:31,720
I'm glad
you're feeling better.

260
00:20:31,790 --> 00:20:35,030
- Get back in bed
- Good thing
your eyesight's failing.

261
00:20:44,670 --> 00:20:47,810
- Hey!
- Mmm. Oh.

262
00:20:47,870 --> 00:20:51,280
- Hey.
- I was hopin'
you'd be here.

263
00:20:51,340 --> 00:20:55,410
My roommate, Mrs. Otis,
said I could visit her family,

264
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:57,430
but I said,
"Thank you kindly,

265
00:20:57,480 --> 00:21:00,120
but I think I might have
my own visitor."

266
00:21:00,190 --> 00:21:02,190
And here you are.

267
00:21:02,250 --> 00:21:04,530
- Well, sit down.
- Thank you.

268
00:21:04,590 --> 00:21:08,130
And doughnuts to boot!
You can't beat that.

269
00:21:08,190 --> 00:21:11,030
- Well, help yourself,
Mrs. Threadgoode.
- Thank you.

270
00:21:11,760 --> 00:21:12,800
How's your friend?

271
00:21:12,870 --> 00:21:14,870
- Mrs. Otis?
- Uh-huh.

272
00:21:14,930 --> 00:21:17,880
- Well, not so good.
- Oh.

273
00:21:17,940 --> 00:21:20,680
Looks like I won't be
gettin' home for quite a while,

274
00:21:20,740 --> 00:21:24,190
and I sure miss it.

275
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:27,520
Funny what you miss
when you're away from home.

276
00:21:27,580 --> 00:21:29,990
I miss
the smell of coffee...

277
00:21:30,050 --> 00:21:32,860
and bacon fryin'.

278
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:37,430
Oh, what I wouldn't give for a
plate of fried green tomatoes...

279
00:21:37,490 --> 00:21:40,200
like we used to have
at the cafe.

280
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:42,670
Ooh!

281
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:49,270
I never told you
about the cafe,
did I?

282
00:21:49,330 --> 00:21:51,280
No, ma'am.

283
00:21:51,340 --> 00:21:55,950
Oh, well...
now let me back up a bit.

284
00:21:56,010 --> 00:22:01,260
You see, Idgie never
quite got over losing Buddy.

285
00:22:03,580 --> 00:22:06,650
She hardly
ever come home.

286
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:09,600
Only Big George
knew how to find her.

287
00:22:09,660 --> 00:22:14,410
She just didn't seem to care
about anythin' anymore.

288
00:22:14,460 --> 00:22:16,410
Then, one summer day

289
00:22:18,300 --> 00:22:20,940
I'll see you,
Grady Kilgore,

290
00:22:21,010 --> 00:22:23,080
and I'll
raise you twenty.

291
00:22:23,140 --> 00:22:25,710
You ain't got nothin'!

292
00:22:25,780 --> 00:22:29,090
Maybe I do and
maybe I don't.

293
00:22:29,150 --> 00:22:33,390
Put your money where
your mouth is, Mr. Sheriff.

294
00:22:37,420 --> 00:22:40,060
Well, look what
the cat drug in!

295
00:22:40,130 --> 00:22:44,010
I came to talk to you.

296
00:22:44,060 --> 00:22:46,440
You're gonna have to wait.
I'm busy.

297
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:49,110
Come on, Grady, this
is your big chance.
You in or out?

298
00:22:49,170 --> 00:22:51,620
I'll make you
a rich man.

299
00:22:51,670 --> 00:22:54,670
You just bluffin' again
as usual

300
00:22:54,740 --> 00:22:57,740
I'm afraid you're gonna
have to excuse Idgie.
She's goin' home for dinner.

301
00:22:57,810 --> 00:22:59,980
- Say good-bye, Idgie.
- Where you goin'?

302
00:23:00,050 --> 00:23:04,430
- Where the hell you goin'
with my money?
- We're goin' home!

303
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:08,430
- Who are you to boss me around?
- The one holdin' your money!

304
00:23:08,490 --> 00:23:10,440
Give it back.

305
00:23:10,490 --> 00:23:12,630
Now, get in the car.

306
00:23:14,490 --> 00:23:17,730
All right.
I'll get in the car.

307
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:20,300
You win!

308
00:23:20,370 --> 00:23:23,350
Come on.

309
00:23:23,400 --> 00:23:24,970
Sucker!

310
00:23:25,040 --> 00:23:27,080
I'll leave when I want!

311
00:23:27,140 --> 00:23:30,950
I don't know how you can break
your mother's heart like you do.

312
00:23:31,010 --> 00:23:33,180
I'm not doin' anything
to my mother.

313
00:23:33,250 --> 00:23:35,820
Oh, no? Why do you think
I'm here for the summer?

314
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:39,260
Your mother was so worried,
she thought I might be able
to talk some sense into you.

315
00:23:39,320 --> 00:23:41,660
But you're too busy
being selfish!

316
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:44,700
What are you
talkin' about?

317
00:23:44,760 --> 00:23:48,470
You're not the only one
who lost Buddy.

318
00:23:48,530 --> 00:23:50,640
We all miss him...

319
00:23:50,700 --> 00:23:53,580
but turning your back on
your family is not gonna help.

320
00:23:55,940 --> 00:23:58,010
What's he got to do
with anything?

321
00:23:58,070 --> 00:24:02,210
I oaks like you 're
the one with the problem
forgetting my brother.

322
00:24:06,580 --> 00:24:09,080
Why just ten miles a way ..

323
00:24:09,150 --> 00:24:11,060
Down by the river,

324
00:24:11,120 --> 00:24:13,360
there lurks
a den of the devil...

325
00:24:13,420 --> 00:24:17,270
Where liquor
and gamblin'...

326
00:24:17,320 --> 00:24:20,170
and sin abide!

327
00:24:25,470 --> 00:24:28,750
Let's turn to page 53
in our hymnal.

328
00:24:34,840 --> 00:24:37,840
Yoo-hoo!

329
00:24:37,910 --> 00:24:42,720
Big George thought
I might find you here.

330
00:24:45,590 --> 00:24:50,440
If you give me a chance,
a chance to get to know you,

331
00:24:50,490 --> 00:24:54,230
maybe it'll be fun!

332
00:24:54,290 --> 00:24:57,700
Fun?

333
00:24:57,760 --> 00:25:01,040
Idgie,just spend
some time with me.

334
00:25:01,100 --> 00:25:03,050
Please?

335
00:25:03,100 --> 00:25:05,050
Suit yourself.

336
00:25:05,740 --> 00:25:08,410
You sure you don't
wanna back out?

337
00:25:08,480 --> 00:25:11,690
- It's not too late.
- I'm sure.

338
00:25:11,750 --> 00:25:14,090
Here, hold this.

339
00:25:16,080 --> 00:25:18,790
Tell me now,
you like trains?

340
00:25:18,850 --> 00:25:22,660
- Yes.
- Good.

341
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:26,630
We'll get along
just fine!

342
00:25:28,130 --> 00:25:31,630
Boy, did we
luck out tonight.

343
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:36,740
Hop in.

344
00:25:36,800 --> 00:25:39,340
Hop?

345
00:25:39,410 --> 00:25:42,450
Oh. Give me
your hand.

346
00:25:42,510 --> 00:25:44,990
Put your foot
up there.

347
00:25:54,290 --> 00:25:56,430
Hold that.

348
00:25:57,320 --> 00:26:00,130
Ooo-ooo!
Look at all this!

349
00:26:04,730 --> 00:26:08,300
Don't you think we should
get off the train?
It's startin' to move.

350
00:26:08,370 --> 00:26:12,180
No. The fun
just started!

351
00:26:15,510 --> 00:26:17,920
You all right?

352
00:26:17,980 --> 00:26:22,220
Well, sometimes I get
a little dizzy lookin' down.

353
00:26:22,280 --> 00:26:24,990
Don't look down.

354
00:26:37,860 --> 00:26:41,640
- What are you doin'?
- Come on. Look.

355
00:26:41,700 --> 00:26:44,610
They're throwin'
away food!

356
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:51,080
You talk about
"give unto others."

357
00:26:51,140 --> 00:26:54,210
Yes, but this food
isn't yours to give.

358
00:27:05,680 --> 00:27:07,320
- More!
- Give me some.

359
00:27:32,640 --> 00:27:36,020
Okay, time to get off.

360
00:27:36,650 --> 00:27:38,630
We gotta jump.

361
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:41,290
Lump?

362
00:27:41,350 --> 00:27:44,420
Yeah jump. The next stop's
five miles down the tracks.

363
00:27:44,490 --> 00:27:46,490
I don't wanna walk
that far back.

364
00:27:46,560 --> 00:27:49,440
Are you crazy?

365
00:27:49,490 --> 00:27:51,870
You're not kiddin'.

366
00:27:51,930 --> 00:27:55,610
Well...

367
00:27:55,670 --> 00:27:58,150
I give up. Jump.-

368
00:27:58,200 --> 00:28:01,480
I'll tell Mama I'm not
a good influence on you-

369
00:28:01,540 --> 00:28:03,820
You'll never jump,
will you?

370
00:28:05,840 --> 00:28:08,980
Don't say "never"
to me.

371
00:28:21,030 --> 00:28:23,810
Towanda!

372
00:28:36,670 --> 00:28:39,280
- You all right?
- I'm fine.

373
00:28:39,340 --> 00:28:42,910
I'm all right.

374
00:28:42,980 --> 00:28:45,120
Ow!

375
00:28:45,180 --> 00:28:47,520
Does this hurt?

376
00:28:47,590 --> 00:28:50,370
Guess so.

377
00:28:50,420 --> 00:28:52,730
- We better get you
to a doc-doctor.
- Shit!

378
00:28:52,790 --> 00:28:54,900
Which way is it?

379
00:28:54,960 --> 00:28:58,570
About two miles
down the tracks.

380
00:28:58,630 --> 00:29:00,870
All right.
let's go.

381
00:29:02,670 --> 00:29:06,170
You'll never be able
to carry me that far.

382
00:29:06,240 --> 00:29:08,950
I know.
Never say never.

383
00:29:09,010 --> 00:29:13,150
I'm not carryin' you.
You're walkin'.

384
00:29:19,080 --> 00:29:23,830
Thank you, Julian.
I owe you one.

385
00:29:35,730 --> 00:29:37,680
Uh. Ow.

386
00:29:37,740 --> 00:29:41,310
Aren't you ready yet?

387
00:29:41,370 --> 00:29:43,480
What?

388
00:29:45,540 --> 00:29:48,610
This doesn't have anything
to do with trains, does it?

389
00:29:49,510 --> 00:29:51,750
You like honey?

390
00:29:51,820 --> 00:29:53,800
Yeah, I like honey.

391
00:29:53,850 --> 00:29:55,850
- Fresh honey?
- Yeah.

392
00:29:55,920 --> 00:29:59,460
Me too.
There it is.

393
00:29:59,520 --> 00:30:03,730
There what... is?

394
00:30:03,790 --> 00:30:07,670
You'll see soon enough.

395
00:30:11,640 --> 00:30:13,880
Now... stay here.

396
00:30:13,940 --> 00:30:16,890
No matter what happens,
don't move.

397
00:30:16,940 --> 00:30:20,220
What are you
gonna do?

398
00:30:55,210 --> 00:30:57,320
Ah.

399
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:35,530
Here you are, madam.
This is for you.

400
00:31:35,590 --> 00:31:39,970
Why did you do that?
You could have been killed.

401
00:31:40,020 --> 00:31:43,520
I'm sorry.

402
00:31:43,590 --> 00:31:46,300
Don't you want
the honey?

403
00:31:46,360 --> 00:31:49,710
I got it
just for you.

404
00:31:49,770 --> 00:31:52,250
It's all right.
I do it all the time.

405
00:31:52,300 --> 00:31:56,080
I never get stung,
honest.

406
00:31:56,140 --> 00:31:58,140
Don't be
mad at me, Ruth.

407
00:31:58,210 --> 00:32:02,120
Idgie.
I'm not mad at you.

408
00:32:02,180 --> 00:32:04,750
No foolin'?

409
00:32:11,560 --> 00:32:14,270
Is it bad,
what I did?

410
00:32:14,320 --> 00:32:16,660
No.

411
00:32:16,730 --> 00:32:18,900
I thought I might
be crazy or somethin'.

412
00:32:18,960 --> 00:32:21,770
No, no.

413
00:32:21,830 --> 00:32:25,510
I've heard there were people
who could charm bees.

414
00:32:25,570 --> 00:32:29,210
I've just never
seen it done...
before today.

415
00:32:31,110 --> 00:32:35,490
You're just a bee charmer,
Idgie Threadgoode.

416
00:32:35,550 --> 00:32:40,020
That's what you are,
a bee charmer.

417
00:32:40,080 --> 00:32:42,820
Here, you want
to taste it?

418
00:32:48,960 --> 00:32:51,700
"Satan started to laugh
at job's devotion.

419
00:32:51,760 --> 00:32:57,010
"He bet God that job would
never have so much faith...

420
00:32:57,070 --> 00:32:59,180
"if he didn't have
so many blessings.

421
00:32:59,240 --> 00:33:03,120
"He went on and on
so long and so much
that God finally agreed...

422
00:33:03,170 --> 00:33:05,880
"to let Satan
put Job to a test.

423
00:33:05,940 --> 00:33:09,080
"Suddenly from bein'
on top of the world,

424
00:33:09,150 --> 00:33:12,790
Job was plunged down
into the deepest pits
of misery."

425
00:33:14,820 --> 00:33:17,560
Surprise!

426
00:33:19,820 --> 00:33:21,770
Idgie Threadgoode!

427
00:33:21,830 --> 00:33:23,780
Tonight we're gonna have
a real party.

428
00:33:23,830 --> 00:33:26,070
Drink this... and then,
we're gonna play some poker.

429
00:33:26,130 --> 00:33:30,010
I don't know
how to play poker
and I never drink...

430
00:33:30,070 --> 00:33:32,070
but thank you anyway.

431
00:33:37,210 --> 00:33:39,710
Here comes the windup.

432
00:33:39,780 --> 00:33:42,120
Burn that ball in here.
Burn 'em in here!

433
00:33:42,180 --> 00:33:46,560
- Right in the pocket.
- I don't know how
to bat.

434
00:33:46,620 --> 00:33:49,430
And you don't drink,
either.

435
00:33:49,490 --> 00:33:52,600
- It's gonna be a spitter.
- Hold the bat and swing

436
00:33:52,660 --> 00:33:54,400
Spitter?

437
00:33:54,460 --> 00:33:57,670
- She gonna spit at me?
- She's gonna spit on the ball

438
00:33:57,730 --> 00:34:00,940
Swing that bat!
Take another crack at it.

439
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:03,170
I'm gonna take
another crack at it.

440
00:34:03,230 --> 00:34:06,440
Get 'em in here.

441
00:34:13,940 --> 00:34:16,750
Now run, Ruth.
Run!

442
00:34:16,810 --> 00:34:18,810
Come on
around the bases!

443
00:34:18,880 --> 00:34:20,880
Don't kiss everybody.
Run!

444
00:34:20,950 --> 00:34:23,990
I have never had
so much fun...

445
00:34:24,050 --> 00:34:26,390
in my whole life.

446
00:34:26,460 --> 00:34:29,770
I even got a home run.

447
00:34:29,830 --> 00:34:32,810
A clean one
at that!

448
00:34:32,860 --> 00:34:36,070
A straight beats
three of a kind.

449
00:34:41,170 --> 00:34:45,410
You know,
poker isn't half bad.

450
00:34:45,480 --> 00:34:47,650
What's your mother
gonna say...

451
00:34:47,710 --> 00:34:51,090
when she sees us both...
drunk?

452
00:34:51,150 --> 00:34:55,060
- You gotta stop worrying
about what people think.
- I know.

453
00:34:55,120 --> 00:34:57,120
You've always done
the right thing.

454
00:34:57,190 --> 00:35:00,640
You took care of your daddy,
the preacher, when he took sick.

455
00:35:00,690 --> 00:35:04,570
You take care of all the kids
over at the church school.

456
00:35:04,630 --> 00:35:07,370
You're gonna
take care of your mama.

457
00:35:07,430 --> 00:35:10,970
And I'm gonna marry
the man I'm supposed to.

458
00:35:11,030 --> 00:35:13,310
You gettin' married?

459
00:35:13,370 --> 00:35:17,650
As soon as
the summer's over.

460
00:35:21,180 --> 00:35:24,890
Oh, am I
gonna miss you.

461
00:35:24,950 --> 00:35:28,090
This is
the best birthday...

462
00:35:28,150 --> 00:35:31,130
I ever had.

463
00:35:43,670 --> 00:35:47,280
Ruth invited Idgie
to the weddin',

464
00:35:50,790 --> 00:35:55,070
Now, Mama Jamison,
you put that down.

465
00:35:55,130 --> 00:35:57,740
Oh, my Lord!

466
00:36:04,240 --> 00:36:06,380
During these next few weeks,

467
00:36:06,440 --> 00:36:10,790
we will be learning to reclaim
our own power as women!

468
00:36:10,850 --> 00:36:12,960
Hallelujah!

469
00:36:13,010 --> 00:36:17,790
And tonight, we're gonna
begin to explore...

470
00:36:17,850 --> 00:36:20,060
our own femaleness...

471
00:36:20,120 --> 00:36:24,690
by examining the source
of our strength...

472
00:36:24,760 --> 00:36:27,140
and our separateness.

473
00:36:27,200 --> 00:36:29,180
Our vaginas.

474
00:36:31,130 --> 00:36:33,940
So if ya'll will just
slip off your panties...

475
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:37,540
and straddle your mirrors.

476
00:36:37,610 --> 00:36:40,280
Ms. Couch!

477
00:36:40,340 --> 00:36:43,790
Ms. Couch!

478
00:36:43,850 --> 00:36:48,230
Um, I need to be excused
for a minute.

479
00:36:48,280 --> 00:36:52,350
Um, Missy, could you come
with me to the ladies' room?

480
00:36:52,420 --> 00:36:56,160
- Do you find this threatening?
- Uh, well, um-

481
00:36:56,220 --> 00:37:00,360
- do you have a problem
with your sexuality?
- No, ma'am.

482
00:37:00,430 --> 00:37:03,470
But I do have a problem
with my girdle.

483
00:37:28,220 --> 00:37:31,790
All right, fried chicken!
My favorite.

484
00:37:37,670 --> 00:37:39,810
Ed?

485
00:37:39,870 --> 00:37:42,940
Ed?

486
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:47,510
Those classes I've been taking
aren't helpin' us one bit.

487
00:37:47,580 --> 00:37:50,250
Let's go to Florida...

488
00:37:50,310 --> 00:37:52,650
like when
we got married.

489
00:37:52,710 --> 00:37:56,060
Kyle's gone,
busy with his own life.

490
00:37:56,120 --> 00:37:58,120
It'd be
just the two of us.

491
00:37:58,190 --> 00:38:01,140
Well, honey, it's just
the two of us here now.

492
00:38:01,190 --> 00:38:03,900
Boy, you got a good scald
on that chicken!

493
00:38:03,960 --> 00:38:06,960
- I'm tellin' you,
that's really good.
- Thank you.

494
00:38:07,030 --> 00:38:08,980
We could rent a boat...

495
00:38:09,030 --> 00:38:12,710
and drift around
in the hot sun.

496
00:38:12,770 --> 00:38:14,880
What do you
