Yeah.

734
00:57:00,810 --> 00:57:02,760
This one November,

735
00:57:02,810 --> 00:57:04,760
all these ducks
come by...

736
00:57:04,810 --> 00:57:08,090
and they landed
on that lake.

737
00:57:08,150 --> 00:57:12,260
Then the temperature
dropped so fast, the
whole lake just froze.

738
00:57:12,320 --> 00:57:15,360
Then the ducks
took off and took
the lake with 'em.

739
00:57:15,420 --> 00:57:18,230
Now that lake's somewhere
in Georgia, the way I hear it.

740
00:57:18,290 --> 00:57:20,960
Go on now.

741
00:57:34,580 --> 00:57:37,060
God bless you,
ma'am.

742
00:58:06,040 --> 00:58:08,320
Here, try this.

743
00:58:12,080 --> 00:58:16,120
- So what do you think?
- They're okay.

744
00:58:16,180 --> 00:58:19,890
- The truth.
- Well-

745
00:58:22,490 --> 00:58:25,270
They're terrible.

746
00:58:25,330 --> 00:58:30,280
Oh, well, don't be shy.
Tell me how you feel.

747
00:58:30,330 --> 00:58:32,870
I will.

748
00:58:45,550 --> 00:58:47,720
What'd you go
and do that for?

749
00:58:50,520 --> 00:58:53,800
I just thought you needed
a little coolin' off.

750
00:58:53,860 --> 00:58:57,970
You're right.

751
00:59:11,310 --> 00:59:14,720
Try these.

752
00:59:18,550 --> 00:59:21,220
I think we need
to make a little paste.

753
00:59:40,300 --> 00:59:43,040
What in the name
of Christmas are
you two doing?

754
00:59:43,100 --> 00:59:45,050
She's tryin'
to teach me
how to cook.

755
00:59:45,110 --> 00:59:47,990
Look at those
fried green tomatoes.

756
00:59:52,080 --> 00:59:56,430
You better stop this.
I'm gonna have to arrest you
for disorderly conduct.

757
00:59:56,480 --> 00:59:58,960
Arrest us then.
Let me handle this.

758
00:59:59,020 --> 01:00:01,300
- All right.
- Grady.

759
01:00:03,090 --> 01:00:05,590
Ha-ha-ha!

760
01:00:05,660 --> 01:00:09,840
Arrest us.
Go ahead, arrest us.

761
01:00:09,900 --> 01:00:14,280
Ruth, I have to say it.
I believe Idgie's been
a bad influence on ya.

762
01:00:14,340 --> 01:00:17,480
I agree.

763
01:00:56,480 --> 01:00:59,590
I'll be back in a minute.

764
01:00:59,650 --> 01:01:01,720
Y'all keep the show
going till then.

765
01:01:01,780 --> 01:01:03,820
We ain't goin'
nowhere.

766
01:01:04,950 --> 01:01:08,090
- ...down again.
- She's still poorly.

767
01:01:08,160 --> 01:01:11,160
Where's the baby?
Who are you?

768
01:01:14,720 --> 01:01:18,760
I ain't scared
of you! No, sir!

769
01:01:18,830 --> 01:01:22,240
You should be.

770
01:01:31,970 --> 01:01:34,350
Mind your manners, boy!

771
01:01:43,250 --> 01:01:45,630
Grady,

772
01:01:45,690 --> 01:01:48,930
what does Gladys think
of you stayin' out late...

773
01:01:48,990 --> 01:01:53,300
and losin' your money to me
in poker night after night?

774
01:01:54,130 --> 01:01:56,970
She likes it
just fine.

775
01:02:01,530 --> 01:02:04,170
- They got Big George.
- Idgie!

776
01:02:04,240 --> 01:02:06,740
- Let go of him!
- Let me handle this!

777
01:02:06,810 --> 01:02:10,690
We seen how you treat
your niggers around here
and we don't like it.

778
01:02:10,740 --> 01:02:15,020
I'm the law in these parts.
I don't care what you
like or don't like.

779
01:02:15,080 --> 01:02:17,060
Turn him loose.

780
01:02:17,120 --> 01:02:20,330
Don't get riled up,
nigger lover.

781
01:02:20,390 --> 01:02:24,860
You deaf or somethin'?
I said, let him go!

782
01:02:24,920 --> 01:02:27,900
- Before you get yourselves
in a whole lot of trouble!
- Calm down.

783
01:02:27,960 --> 01:02:30,740
We wanted to have
a little get-together...

784
01:02:30,800 --> 01:02:33,780
and make sure we see
eye to eye on some things.

785
01:02:33,830 --> 01:02:37,280
You hear me now?

786
01:02:37,340 --> 01:02:39,380
Let's let him go, boys.

787
01:02:39,440 --> 01:02:41,150
We've had enough fun
for one night.

788
01:02:41,210 --> 01:02:43,160
- Turn him loose.
- Come on.

789
01:02:43,210 --> 01:02:45,190
No, you're gonna
get in trouble.

790
01:02:47,750 --> 01:02:50,290
Well, now,
that's more like it.

791
01:02:50,350 --> 01:02:53,300
Seems I don't recognize
any of you boys.

792
01:02:53,350 --> 01:02:55,590
Y'all ain't from Whistle Stop,
are you?

793
01:02:58,630 --> 01:03:00,700
This ought to do it.

794
01:03:00,760 --> 01:03:03,760
I want to thank you,
Miss Idgie.

795
01:03:03,830 --> 01:03:09,010
Forget it.
You'd have done
the same for me.

796
01:03:09,070 --> 01:03:12,880
Try to get some sleep.

797
01:03:17,680 --> 01:03:20,790
Who the hell
were those assholes?

798
01:03:20,850 --> 01:03:26,130
They's just some old boys
from Georgia come over here
to put a scare in you.

799
01:03:26,190 --> 01:03:28,640
Well, it worked.

800
01:03:28,690 --> 01:03:31,400
One of 'em was here
the other day for something,

801
01:03:31,460 --> 01:03:34,000
seen you sellin' food
to coloreds.

802
01:03:34,060 --> 01:03:38,130
They decided to come back,
shake you up a bit.

803
01:03:38,200 --> 01:03:41,650
I told 'em we don't need
anybody from Georgia
comin' over here...

804
01:03:41,700 --> 01:03:44,240
tellin' us what
we can or cannot do.

805
01:03:44,300 --> 01:03:49,480
They won't be back.
I guaran-gol-damn-tee
you that.

806
01:03:49,540 --> 01:03:52,610
One other thing,
little Miss Smarty-pants,

807
01:03:52,680 --> 01:03:56,960
I do not wear a size 14 shoe...

808
01:03:57,020 --> 01:04:00,590
and I don't
much care for parades,

809
01:04:00,650 --> 01:04:04,260
bedsheets or otherwise.

810
01:04:48,830 --> 01:04:52,180
- Hey there!
- You got to come quick.

811
01:04:52,230 --> 01:04:55,400
Well, the show
has hardly begun.

812
01:04:55,470 --> 01:04:58,210
You got to come quick now.
You hear me?

813
01:05:00,940 --> 01:05:03,250
- Run, get help!
Run, quick!
- Where's the baby?

814
01:05:03,310 --> 01:05:05,350
Never mind.

815
01:05:24,760 --> 01:05:30,300
Excuse me, sir.
I don't believe you
should be goin' anywhere...

816
01:05:30,370 --> 01:05:32,940
with Ruth's baby.

817
01:06:17,250 --> 01:06:19,290
What's he done?

818
01:06:19,350 --> 01:06:23,360
Nothin' that we know of.
We're tryin' to find out
what's been did to him.

819
01:06:23,420 --> 01:06:26,920
He told his hired man he was
comin' to see his wife and baby,

820
01:06:26,990 --> 01:06:31,000
but he ain't never
showed up back home.

821
01:06:31,060 --> 01:06:33,770
Hell, I told him
if he showed up in this town,

822
01:06:33,830 --> 01:06:35,970
we'd all have known.

823
01:06:36,030 --> 01:06:38,480
Looks a little sissified
to me.

824
01:06:38,540 --> 01:06:42,550
From what I hear,
most you boys in Georgia...

825
01:06:42,610 --> 01:06:44,060
are a little light
on your feet

826
01:06:44,110 --> 01:06:47,280
That's the way
I heard it.

827
01:06:47,340 --> 01:06:49,480
Could I interest you
in some pie?

828
01:06:49,550 --> 01:06:53,460
No, ma'am, but that
barbecue sure smells good.

829
01:06:53,520 --> 01:06:56,970
Best damn barbecue
in the state of Alabama.

830
01:07:26,180 --> 01:07:28,820
Here you go.
That's your 4th one today.

831
01:07:28,890 --> 01:07:31,730
I swear you're about
to eat up all my barbecue.

832
01:07:31,790 --> 01:07:34,570
Sit down.

833
01:07:34,630 --> 01:07:37,610
Sit down.

834
01:07:45,240 --> 01:07:47,910
You sure you ain't
never seen this man, boy?

835
01:07:47,970 --> 01:07:51,610
Yes, sir, and I already told ya,
I ain't never seen him.

836
01:07:51,680 --> 01:07:54,180
You'd do anything for
Miss Idgie, wouldn't ya, boy?

837
01:07:56,080 --> 01:07:58,030
Yes, sir.

838
01:08:01,250 --> 01:08:04,860
Would ya kill for her?
Did ya kill for her?

839
01:08:12,230 --> 01:08:14,370
No, sir.

840
01:08:14,430 --> 01:08:19,280
Well, now, maybe
one of these days
you'll tell the truth.

841
01:08:21,310 --> 01:08:24,020
Just remember, we hang
lyin' niggers in Georgia...

842
01:08:24,080 --> 01:08:27,060
just as fast as
they do in Alabama.

843
01:08:27,110 --> 01:08:30,890
Yes, sir, I remember.

844
01:09:08,450 --> 01:09:12,900
Sorry.

845
01:09:12,960 --> 01:09:17,910
- What are ya
doin' in here?
- No milk in the house.

846
01:09:17,960 --> 01:09:20,070
Where were you?

847
01:09:20,130 --> 01:09:23,080
Takin' care of business,
havin' a good time.

848
01:09:25,800 --> 01:09:29,370
I've been thinkin'
maybe I should move on...

849
01:09:32,250 --> 01:09:34,200
You don't believe me.

850
01:09:34,250 --> 01:09:38,820
Right now, I don't know
what to believe.

851
01:09:41,290 --> 01:09:44,600
Believe me when I tell ya
I don't want ya to move out.

852
01:10:10,190 --> 01:10:13,540
Finally.

853
01:10:13,590 --> 01:10:17,330
Thanks, I've been
out here all day.

854
01:10:44,490 --> 01:10:46,900
Excuse me.
I was waiting for that space.

855
01:10:46,960 --> 01:10:51,910
- Yeah? Tough!
- Face it, lady,
we're younger and faster.

856
01:11:12,450 --> 01:11:15,360
Towanda.

857
01:11:18,860 --> 01:11:21,900
Ha-ha-ha-ha!

858
01:11:21,960 --> 01:11:26,880
Yeah!
Whooo!

859
01:11:31,240 --> 01:11:33,720
Towanda!

860
01:11:38,580 --> 01:11:41,390
Yes, ma'am.

861
01:11:41,450 --> 01:11:44,160
Whoooo!

862
01:11:47,150 --> 01:11:50,650
- Help, someone!
- What are you doing?
Are you crazy?

863
01:11:50,720 --> 01:11:55,670
Face it, girls.
I'm older, and I
have more insurance.

864
01:12:04,270 --> 01:12:07,910
I never get mad,
Mrs. Threadgoode.
Never!

865
01:12:07,970 --> 01:12:10,540
The way I was raised
it was bad manners.

866
01:12:10,610 --> 01:12:13,780
Well, I got mad
and it felt terrific.

867
01:12:13,850 --> 01:12:17,160
I felt like I could beat
the shit outta all those punks!

868
01:12:17,220 --> 01:12:19,960
Excuse my language.
just beat 'em to a pulp!

869
01:12:20,020 --> 01:12:22,160
Beat 'em till
they begged for mercy.

870
01:12:22,220 --> 01:12:24,260
Towanda, the avenger!

871
01:12:26,390 --> 01:12:29,960
I'll give half the military
budget to people over 65...

872
01:12:30,030 --> 01:12:32,770
and declare wrinkles
sexually desirable.

873
01:12:32,830 --> 01:12:37,470
Towanda, righter of wrongs,
queen beyond compare!

874
01:12:37,540 --> 01:12:40,850
How many of them
hormones you takin', honey?

875
01:12:56,320 --> 01:12:58,820
what I can't
understand is...

876
01:12:58,890 --> 01:13:02,500
how in the hell
you can hit someone...

877
01:13:02,560 --> 01:13:04,800
six times
by accident.

878
01:13:04,860 --> 01:13:07,900
Oh, Ed, don't make
such a big deal about it.

879
01:13:14,310 --> 01:13:18,850
- What the hell is this?
- A low cholesterol meal.

880
01:13:18,910 --> 01:13:20,860
Happy Valentine's.

881
01:13:24,120 --> 01:13:27,070
My God!
Are you tryin' to kill me?

882
01:13:27,120 --> 01:13:30,400
If I was gonna kill ya,
I'd use my hands.

883
01:13:47,310 --> 01:13:49,920
I'm worried about
my little friend Evelyn.

884
01:13:49,980 --> 01:13:52,550
She said her husband...

885
01:13:52,610 --> 01:13:54,920
will just be watching
his sports on TV...

886
01:13:54,980 --> 01:13:58,150
and she has an urge to hit him
in the head with a baseball bat.

887
01:13:58,220 --> 01:14:01,100
Hell, that
seems normal to me.

888
01:14:01,150 --> 01:14:03,150
- Hi Janeen.
- Mm-hmm

889
01:14:03,220 --> 01:14:05,700
Mrs. Threadgoode, would
you like some crudites?

890
01:14:14,710 --> 01:14:16,660
Buddy.

891
01:14:16,710 --> 01:14:18,660
Everybody
outta the way.

892
01:14:18,710 --> 01:14:22,490
Give him here.
Let him go. I've got him.

893
01:14:24,450 --> 01:14:26,660
Come on. You're
gonna be all right.

894
01:14:26,720 --> 01:14:29,060
Open the door!

895
01:14:29,120 --> 01:14:33,190
Put him in the car.
It's all right, honey

896
01:14:54,420 --> 01:14:56,330
I can understand...

897
01:14:56,380 --> 01:14:58,920
having a funeral
for an arm.

898
01:14:58,990 --> 01:15:02,530
I just don't know why
she insists on callin'
him "Stump."?

899
01:15:02,590 --> 01:15:05,590
She say everybody else gonna
be callin' him that...

900
01:15:05,660 --> 01:15:09,770
so we might just as well
be the first.

901
01:15:09,830 --> 01:15:14,010
Okay, ice cream
and cake for everybody.

902
01:15:14,070 --> 01:15:15,880
Go on.

903
01:15:20,140 --> 01:15:24,150
My daddy always used to say
there was a separate God
for children.

904
01:15:28,020 --> 01:15:31,560
The good Lord was watchin'
over stump that day.

905
01:15:31,620 --> 01:15:35,000
But then it started to rain
that month.

906
01:15:36,840 --> 01:15:39,840
When her husband came back
to get her and take her home,

907
01:15:39,910 --> 01:15:44,550
you and your colored man
murdered him in cold blood.

908
01:15:45,750 --> 01:15:47,350
No, sir.

909
01:15:47,420 --> 01:15:52,700
Well, where were you on the
night of September 30, 1933?

910
01:15:52,760 --> 01:15:55,070
I was at the town hall
doing a show.

911
01:15:55,130 --> 01:15:58,240
- And after that?
- I was at
my mother's house.

912
01:15:58,300 --> 01:16:00,840
Oh, yeah?
Who was with you?

913
01:16:00,900 --> 01:16:05,250
- Just Big George and myself
- What about your mother?
Can she confirm that?

914
01:16:05,300 --> 01:16:07,580
No, sir.
She died a year ago.

915
01:16:07,640 --> 01:16:10,140
I'm sorry to hear that.

916
01:16:10,210 --> 01:16:13,920
But do you expect 12 intelligent
men to believe you,

917
01:16:13,980 --> 01:16:16,620
although one witness is dead and
the other is a colored man,

918
01:16:16,680 --> 01:16:20,090
known to be a worthless,
no-good, lying nigger?

919
01:16:20,150 --> 01:16:22,430
You expect these men
to take your word for it...

920
01:16:22,490 --> 01:16:25,160
just because
you say so?

921
01:16:25,220 --> 01:16:29,760
That's right,
you gump-faced, blown-up,
baboon-assed bastard!

922
01:16:29,830 --> 01:16:33,300
One more outburst
like that...

923
01:16:33,360 --> 01:16:36,860
and I'll hold you
in contempt of court.
You understand?

924
01:16:36,930 --> 01:16:39,740
Yes, sir.

925
01:16:41,440 --> 01:16:45,010
- Oh, Lord.
- Next witness.

926
01:16:47,580 --> 01:16:49,060
Did you know that
you were pregnant'...

927
01:16:53,360 --> 01:16:56,970
of Idgie Threadgoode
and her colored man,
known as Big George,

928
01:16:57,030 --> 01:17:00,810
on the night
of September 30, 1933?

929
01:17:00,870 --> 01:17:02,850
Yes, sir,
I do.

930
01:17:02,900 --> 01:17:05,350
It has been
suggested here...

931
01:17:05,400 --> 01:17:08,870
that she and her colored man
were at her mother's house.

932
01:17:08,940 --> 01:17:13,180
- Can you confirm that?
- No, sir.
That is a lie.

933
01:17:13,250 --> 01:17:15,990
Oh, shit.

934
01:17:16,050 --> 01:17:19,290
It has been my habit
to write all the dates...

935
01:17:19,350 --> 01:17:22,300
Of the activities of
the church in my Bible.

936
01:17:22,350 --> 01:17:27,030
I show that the night
of September 30, 1933...

937
01:17:27,090 --> 01:17:30,130
was the start of our
annual revival...

938
01:17:30,200 --> 01:17:32,980
down at the
Baptist campground.

939
01:17:33,030 --> 01:17:35,140
Sister Threadgoode
was there...

940
01:17:35,200 --> 01:17:39,240
along with her hired man,
George Pullman,

941
01:17:39,310 --> 01:17:43,450
who was in charge of the
barbecue as he has been...

942
01:17:43,510 --> 01:17:46,180
- for the last ten years.
- Objection.

943
01:17:46,250 --> 01:17:50,790
That doesn't mean anything.
Murder could've taken place any
time the next couple of clays.

944
01:17:50,850 --> 01:17:55,890
- Have you ever been to one
of our revivals, sir?
- Well, no.

945
01:17:55,960 --> 01:17:58,030
Do you attend church
regularly, sir?

946
01:17:58,090 --> 01:18:00,300
'Course I do.

947
01:18:00,360 --> 01:18:04,900
Good. Well, maybe if you
attended one of our revivals,

948
01:18:04,960 --> 01:18:07,340
you'd know
they last three days...

949
01:18:07,400 --> 01:18:09,740
and three nights,
Your Honor.

950
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:14,980
Approach the bench.

951
01:18:15,040 --> 01:18:19,750
Percy, it don't look like
you got a case at all.

952
01:18:19,810 --> 01:18:22,380
In the first place,
there's no body.

953
01:18:22,450 --> 01:18:25,730
Second, we got us a preacher
nobody's gonna dispute.

954
01:18:34,840 --> 01:18:37,750
See you in church,
Sister?

955
01:18:38,650 --> 01:18:40,890
Reverend.

956
01:18:40,950 --> 01:18:45,260
I can't believe he
actually swore on a Bible.

957
01:18:45,320 --> 01:18:47,270
Well, not really.

958
01:18:47,320 --> 01:18:49,320
If that judge
had looked closer,

959
01:18:49,390 --> 01:18:52,460
he'd have seen it was really
a copy of Moby Dick.

960
01:18:54,500 --> 01:18:58,920
- But why did he do it?
- For the sheer joy of
seeing you in church again...

961
01:18:58,970 --> 01:19:01,810
which I suggested to him
might be your penance.

962
01:19:01,870 --> 01:19:04,510
- You didn't promise him,
did you?
- Yes, ma'am, I did.

963
01:19:04,570 --> 01:19:06,520
And I never
break my word.

964
01:19:06,580 --> 01:19:10,960
If I live 1,000 years,
I will never forgive you.

965
01:19:11,010 --> 01:19:15,190
I don't know what's worse,
church or jail.

966
01:19:26,160 --> 01:19:29,300
There now.
Don't you look pretty?

967
01:19:29,360 --> 01:19:31,500
Oh, yes, honey.

968
01:19:31,570 --> 01:19:36,250
You'll have me
lookin' like Ginger Rogers
before you're done.

969
01:19:36,310 --> 01:19:40,550
Don't let Mr. Dunaway see me.
He's liable to go wild.

970
01:19:42,040 --> 01:19:45,280
I'm glad to see
you're in a good mood.

971
01:19:45,350 --> 01:19:48,490
You've slimmed down quite a bit
in the last few weeks.

972
01:19:48,550 --> 01:19:52,860
I'm just so happy Big George
and Idgie got off.

973
01:20:15,640 --> 01:20:18,680
Evelyn, what in the hell
are you doing?

974
01:20:18,750 --> 01:20:21,660
I need some light
and air.

975
01:20:21,720 --> 01:20:24,930
Why don't you take
one of your walks
or your jog...

976
01:20:24,990 --> 01:20:28,530
or whatever it is
you do?

977
01:20:28,590 --> 01:20:31,500
There's no dinner
either!

978
01:20:31,560 --> 01:20:36,010
Ed, you have any idea
why I've been goin'
to all these classes?

979
01:20:36,060 --> 01:20:39,600
- No.
- I've been trying to save
our marriage.

980
01:20:39,670 --> 01:20:41,710
What's the point
of my tryin'...

981
01:20:41,770 --> 01:20:46,450
if you're gonna sit on
your butt drinking beer...

982
01:20:46,510 --> 01:20:49,350
and watching baseball,
basketball, football...

983
01:20:49,410 --> 01:20:52,550
bowling and hockey
and golf...

984
01:20:52,610 --> 01:20:56,490
and Challenge
of the Gladiators?

985
01:21:02,190 --> 01:21:06,730
Mrs. Couch, I'm Sue,
Mrs. Otis' daughter-in-law.

986
01:21:06,800 --> 01:21:10,250
How are you?
I've heard about you
from Mrs. Threadgoode.

987
01:21:10,300 --> 01:21:14,010
She is so sweet. She's been
lookin' after my mother-in-law.

988
01:21:14,070 --> 01:21:16,850
Now, how is
Mrs. Otis doin',
by the way?

989
01:21:16,910 --> 01:21:21,380
Much better, thank you.
It takes time getting used
to a strange place.

990
01:21:21,440 --> 01:21:25,480
I'm glad to hear it.
Mrs. Threadgoode's
been anxious to get home.

991
01:21:25,550 --> 01:21:29,760
Mrs. Couch, Mrs. Threadgoode
doesn't have a house anymore.

992
01:21:29,820 --> 01:21:33,290
- They tore
that down.
- What?

993
01:21:33,350 --> 01:21:37,590
They had to.
It was falling apart,
and it was condemned.

994
01:21:37,660 --> 01:21:40,610
Oh, no.

995
01:21:40,660 --> 01:21:44,870
- Does she know that?
- No, well, we didn't see
any point in telling her.

996
01:21:44,930 --> 01:21:47,430
It would just break her heart,
poor old thing

997
01:21:47,500 --> 01:21:51,450
But I am so glad
I got a chance to meet you.

998
01:21:51,510 --> 01:21:54,720
You take care of yourself now.
Bye-bye.

999
01:23:04,680 --> 01:23:06,990
Oh, Evelyn. hey!

1000
01:23:07,050 --> 01:23:09,530
Hey-

1001
01:23:09,580 --> 01:23:11,960
Do you like
my roses?

1002
01:23:12,020 --> 01:23:15,370
Since I can't get home
to look at my own roses...

1003
01:23:15,420 --> 01:23:17,800
I made myself
a paper garden.

1004
01:23:17,860 --> 01:23:21,360
- Got everything
but the bugs.
- They're lovely.

1005
01:23:21,430 --> 01:23:24,710
- You been here long?
- Happy birthday!

1006
01:23:24,770 --> 01:23:27,270
- Oh!
- I shouldn't
have woken you up.

1007
01:23:27,340 --> 01:23:31,620
'Course you should've.
Don't you never let me sleep
through a visitor's day, honey.

1008
01:23:31,670 --> 01:23:36,420
- I look forward to them all week.
- So do I, Mrs. Threadgoode.

1009
01:23:36,480 --> 01:23:39,830
Oh! I can't believe
you remembered.

1010
01:23:39,880 --> 01:23:44,090
You made me
fried green tomatoes!

1011
01:23:46,520 --> 01:23:48,560
Mmm!
They're delicious.

1012
01:23:48,620 --> 01:23:51,970
- It's your recipe.
Are they cold?
- No.
They're just the way...

1013
01:23:52,030 --> 01:23:56,310
- we used to have 'em
at the Whistle Stop Cafe.
- Mmm!

1014
01:23:56,360 --> 01:24:00,310
You couldn't be sweeter to me
if you was my own daughter.

1015
01:24:00,370 --> 01:24:02,540
Here's your napkin.

1016
01:24:02,600 --> 01:24:04,640
And wait-wait-wait.

1017
01:24:04,710 --> 01:24:07,280
Queen, queen.

1018
01:24:10,450 --> 01:24:14,590
You know,
I don't feel 83.

1019
01:24:14,650 --> 01:24:18,790
It sorta slipped up on me.

1020
01:24:20,890 --> 01:24:24,340
I never expected
to live this long.

1021
01:24:24,390 --> 01:24:30,000
'Course, the Lord takes us home
when he wants us.

1022
01:24:39,010 --> 01:24:42,650
Are you all right?

1023
01:24:42,710 --> 01:24:45,050
I was thinking
about Ruth.

1024
01:24:45,110 --> 01:24:47,920
After the trial
was over,

1025
01:24:47,980 --> 01:24:50,190
Everything went back
to normal...

1026
01:24:50,250 --> 01:24:54,030
till that fall
when Ruth lost her appetite.

1027
01:24:54,090 --> 01:24:56,660
By the time Doc Hadley
looked at her,

1028
01:24:56,720 --> 01:25:00,930
he said the cancer was so bad
she only had a couple of weeks.

1029
01:25:01,000 --> 01:25:03,740
Well, we moved her
to the Threadgoode house...

1030
01:25:03,800 --> 01:25:08,650
and put her downstairs
so she'd be more comfortable.

1031
01:25:08,700 --> 01:25:13,210
Sipsey moved in with her
and never left her side.

1032
01:25:13,270 --> 01:25:15,410
Hold on, baby
I'm right here.

1033
01:25:15,480 --> 01:25:20,160
Idgie just prayed
for a miracle.

1034
01:25:39,430 --> 01:25:42,900
Now, listen to me.

1035
01:25:42,970 --> 01:25:45,510
Make sure he graduates.

1036
01:25:45,570 --> 01:25:49,780
And don't... let him
come to the funeral.

1037
01:25:49,840 --> 01:25:52,510
I don't want him going
through that mess.

1038
01:25:52,580 --> 01:25:55,890
Would you quit talkin'
like that?

1039
01:25:55,950 --> 01:25:58,450
What funeral?

1040
01:25:58,520 --> 01:26:00,900
You're gonna be back on
your feet feelin' just fine...

1041
01:26:00,960 --> 01:26:03,630
in just a few days.

1042
01:26:03,690 --> 01:26:06,600
Just you wait.

1043
01:26:06,660 --> 01:26:09,800
Oh, what's the matter,
son?

1044
01:26:15,640 --> 01:26:19,320
Well,
let's go for a walk.

1045
01:26:20,010 --> 01:26:21,610
Did you get
into a fight?

1046
01:26:21,680 --> 01:26:24,390
I got punched
in the nose.

1047
01:26:24,450 --> 01:26:27,950
I can't play
like everyone else.

1048
01:26:28,020 --> 01:26:31,560
Did I ever tell you the
story about... the oysters?

1049
01:26:31,620 --> 01:26:34,100
All the millions of 'em
just lying around-

1050
01:26:34,160 --> 01:26:39,010
- And God put sand in one of 'em,
and it makes a pearl.
- Oh.

1051
01:26:40,760 --> 01:26:43,430
Did I ever tell you about
Eva's three-legged dog?

1052
01:26:43,500 --> 01:26:45,610
How it never felt sorry
for itself...

1053
01:26:45,670 --> 01:26:49,310
and howl ought to be
smarter than a dumb dog
and not feel sorry for myself.

1054
01:26:51,110 --> 01:26:54,460
You listen to everything
I say, don't you?

1055
01:26:54,510 --> 01:26:57,490
You get real mad at me
when I don't.

1056
01:26:57,550 --> 01:26:59,260
Well,

1057
01:27:01,720 --> 01:27:04,720
you know about
your mama.

1058
01:27:04,790 --> 01:27:07,290
She's sick.

1059
01:27:07,360 --> 01:27:09,400
Mm-hmm.

1060
01:27:10,930 --> 01:27:14,380
See, now is the time
for courage.

1061
01:27:14,430 --> 01:27:18,140
I guess you already know
that there are...

1062
01:27:18,200 --> 01:27:21,200
angels masqueradin' as people
walkin' around this planet,

1063
01:27:21,270 --> 01:27:24,440
and your mom's
the bravest one of those.

1064
01:27:28,710 --> 01:27:30,820
Come here.

1065
01:27:38,520 --> 01:27:40,930
Mama, I can hit!
You should see me.

1066
01:27:40,990 --> 01:27:43,800
Idgie, she hit me in
the back with a curveball.

1067
01:27:43,860 --> 01:27:46,030
I didn't duck,
and I hardly cried.

1068
01:27:46,090 --> 01:27:49,560
She hit you?

1069
01:27:49,630 --> 01:27:53,640
Well, she did that
to me once too,

1070
01:27:53,700 --> 01:27:56,480
but I think
I did cry.

1071
01:27:58,370 --> 01:28:02,340
Mama, I'm sorry
if you're sad.

1072
01:28:02,410 --> 01:28:04,720
Well,

1073
01:28:04,780 --> 01:28:07,890
give me a big kiss then,
and I'll never be sad again.

1074
01:28:15,420 --> 01:28:18,330
And you best not be sad
neither.

1075
01:28:18,390 --> 01:28:21,630
You understand?

1076
01:28:21,700 --> 01:28:23,650
You promise?

1077
01:28:23,700 --> 01:28:25,740
Promise.

1078
01:28:25,800 --> 01:28:29,750
Attaboy.
You go and wash up.

1079
01:28:53,560 --> 01:28:55,600
Sweet baby.

1080
01:28:59,570 --> 01:29:02,850
You two
be alone now.

1081
01:29:03,540 --> 01:29:07,220
Hey, girl.

1082
01:29:09,710 --> 01:29:11,780
No.

1083
01:29:13,710 --> 01:29:16,780
That's nice.

1084
01:29:17,790 --> 01:29:21,500
Will you do one thing
for me?

1085
01:29:21,560 --> 01:29:25,170
- Yeah, anything.
- Be good to yourself.

1086
01:29:25,230 --> 01:29:28,180
Even...

1087
01:29:28,230 --> 01:29:30,770
settle down if
you can find someone...

1088
01:29:30,830 --> 01:29:33,570
who can beat you
in poker.

1089
01:29:41,280 --> 01:29:46,250
There's so many things
I want to say to you.

1090
01:29:46,310 --> 01:29:48,850
No.

1091
01:29:49,680 --> 01:29:52,350
I love your stories.

1092
01:29:52,420 --> 01:29:55,370
Tell me a story,
Idgie.

1093
01:29:58,230 --> 01:30:02,080
Oh, God.

1094
01:30:02,130 --> 01:30:05,240
Go on,
you old' bee charmer.

1095
01:30:05,300 --> 01:30:08,980
Tell me
a good tall tale.

1096
01:30:10,370 --> 01:30:14,080
Tell me the one
about the lake.

1097
01:30:15,380 --> 01:30:20,020
- What lake?
- The one...
that used to be here.

1098
01:30:22,150 --> 01:30:24,100
Oh.

1099
01:30:26,150 --> 01:30:29,720
Well, that was
just a lie.

1100
01:30:29,790 --> 01:30:32,570
I know that, fool.

1101
01:30:32,630 --> 01:30:34,700
Tell me anyway.

1102
01:30:34,760 --> 01:30:38,170
Tell me the story.

1103
01:30:39,730 --> 01:30:43,180
Well...

1104
01:30:45,210 --> 01:30:47,690
one time...

1105
01:30:47,740 --> 01:30:50,550
there was this lake.

1106
01:30:54,980 --> 01:30:59,360
And, uh, it was
right outside of town.

1107
01:30:59,420 --> 01:31:04,870
We used to go
fishin' and swimmin'
and canoein' in it.

1108
01:31:04,930 --> 01:31:08,170
And see,
one November...

1109
01:31:08,230 --> 01:31:10,540
this big ﬂock
of ducks...

1110
01:31:10,600 --> 01:31:15,640
came in and landed
on that lake and, uh,

1111
01:31:15,700 --> 01:31:20,550
and then the temperature
dropped so fast that the
lake just froze right there.

1112
01:31:20,610 --> 01:31:22,890
And the, uh,

1113
01:31:22,940 --> 01:31:26,720
the ducks, they...

1114
01:31:26,780 --> 01:31:30,960
ﬂew off, you see,
and took that lake with 'em.

1115
01:31:31,020 --> 01:31:34,260
And, uh.

1116
01:31:34,320 --> 01:31:39,330
Now they say that lake is
somewhere over in Georgia.

1117
01:31:39,390 --> 01:31:42,460
Can you imagine?

1118
01:32:40,150 --> 01:32:43,430
It's all right,
honey.

1119
01:32:43,490 --> 01:32:46,030
Let her go.

1120
01:32:46,090 --> 01:32:49,470
Let her go.

1121
01:32:49,530 --> 01:32:53,770
You know,
Miss Ruth was a lady.

1122
01:32:53,830 --> 01:32:57,110
And a lady
always knows...

1123
01:32:57,170 --> 01:33:00,170
when to leave.

1124
01:33:05,680 --> 01:33:09,790
When I think on our
departed sister, Ruth Jamison,

1125
01:33:09,850 --> 01:33:12,960
I'm reminded of our
Lord's Sermon on the Mount...

1126
01:33:13,020 --> 01:33:15,500
and how his teachings-

1127
01:33:15,560 --> 01:33:20,010
It's funny how strong
Ruth affected everyone.

1128
01:33:20,060 --> 01:33:23,470
even Smokey Lonesome.

1129
01:33:23,530 --> 01:33:26,200
When he died
a few years back...

1130
01:33:26,270 --> 01:33:28,980
he had one possession
on him,

1131
01:33:29,040 --> 01:33:31,650
A picture of Ruth.

1132
01:33:33,010 --> 01:33:37,120
He was in love with her
from the first time he saw her.

1133
01:33:37,180 --> 01:33:40,060
We all were.

1134
01:33:46,020 --> 01:33:48,500
I shouldn't
a-told you this.

1135
01:33:50,420 --> 01:33:54,390
I hate death.
It scares me so.

1136
01:33:54,460 --> 01:33:57,000
Death is nothin'
to be afraid of!

1137
01:33:57,060 --> 01:34:00,130
Look at me. I'm at
the jumpin'-off place,

1138
01:34:00,200 --> 01:34:03,440
and I ain't afraid
one bit.

1139
01:34:03,500 --> 01:34:07,210
Oh, Ninny,
you're so brave.

1140
01:34:08,780 --> 01:34:12,730
Ruth and Idgie were brave,
not me.

1141
01:34:12,780 --> 01:34:16,160
I wouldn't be afraid
of death if I was you.

1142
01:34:16,220 --> 01:34:21,170
I'd be more afraid of driving
in rush-hour traffic.

1143
01:36:16,370 --> 01:36:19,370
Hi, honey.
Look what I got you.

1144
01:36:19,440 --> 01:36:21,480
Ah...

1145
01:36:21,540 --> 01:36:25,010
Ed, how sweet!

1146
01:36:25,080 --> 01:36:27,530
- Lilies!
My favorite.
- Yeah.

1147
01:36:27,580 --> 01:36:30,720
I know.
Sometimes I even amaze myself.

1148
01:36:30,780 --> 01:36:34,890
- What's the occasion?
- Oh, honey,
I just...

1149
01:36:34,960 --> 01:36:37,940
feel sorry about
the past few months.

1150
01:36:37,990 --> 01:36:42,000
I don't know what
you're really up to and
what's going on with you,

1151
01:36:42,060 --> 01:36:46,480
but I guess I could've been
more helpful with your job
and everything, you know.

1152
01:36:47,700 --> 01:36:49,580
Well, why are you...

1153
01:36:49,640 --> 01:36:52,620
puttin' up this wall
where you just tore one down?

1154
01:36:52,670 --> 01:36:55,810
Well...
I changed my mind.

1155
01:36:55,880 --> 01:36:58,660
I don't mean to seem
dense or anything,

1156
01:36:58,710 --> 01:37:02,950
- but what's changed?
- The air and the light.

1157
01:37:05,320 --> 01:37:07,930
- Ed-
- Hmm?

1158
01:37:07,990 --> 01:37:10,470
You remember how
you used to tell me...

1159
01:37:10,520 --> 01:37:13,260
you always wanted
two women in your house?

1160
01:37:13,330 --> 01:37:15,640
Oh, God.

1161
01:37:15,700 --> 01:37:17,370
Yeah.

1162
01:37:17,430 --> 01:37:19,470
Well...

1163
01:37:19,530 --> 01:37:22,480
what if I was
the younger of the two?

1164
01:37:22,540 --> 01:37:26,080
I don't believe
I get your drift.

1165
01:37:26,140 --> 01:37:30,680
I want something
more than I've ever
wanted anything before.

1166
01:37:30,740 --> 01:37:33,520
I want to bring
Mrs. Threadgoode...

1167
01:37:33,580 --> 01:37:35,790
to our home.

1168
01:37:35,850 --> 01:37:38,490
I want her
to live here with us.

1169
01:37:38,550 --> 01:37:41,050
I want to give her the love
she's given me.

1170
01:37:41,120 --> 01:37:45,300
You're kiddin' me, aren't you?
I'm absolutely serious.

1171
01:37:45,360 --> 01:37:50,210
That's why I'm puttin' the
wall to Kyle's room back up.

1172
01:37:50,260 --> 01:37:53,330
Well, honey, this isn't
something you're just go and do.

1173
01:37:53,400 --> 01:37:56,070
I mean,
she's an old woman.

1174
01:37:56,140 --> 01:37:59,380
What if she got sick?
Who's gonna take care of her?

1175
01:37:59,440 --> 01:38:01,150
I will!

1176
01:38:01,210 --> 01:38:03,210
I can't leave her
in that place.

1177
01:38:03,280 --> 01:38:07,190
She's not a stray cat.
Hell, she isn't even family.

1178
01:38:07,250 --> 01:38:10,320
- She's family to me.
- Now, Evelyn.

1179
01:38:11,150 --> 01:38:14,220
Evelyn?

1180
01:38:14,290 --> 01:38:16,170
Honey?

1181
01:38:16,220 --> 01:38:18,220
Ah, look...

1182
01:38:18,290 --> 01:38:22,530
have you mentioned this
harebrained idea to her?

1183
01:38:22,600 --> 01:38:25,670
- Not yet.
- Well, good!

1184
01:38:25,730 --> 01:38:28,210
Then we'll just pretend
it never happened.

1185
01:38:28,270 --> 01:38:31,310
I'm making my own money.
I'll pay for everything.

1186
01:38:31,370 --> 01:38:34,940
You don't have to do
a thing.

1187
01:38:35,010 --> 01:38:37,510
Evelyn...

1188
01:38:37,580 --> 01:38:40,060
it's never
gonna happen.

1189
01:38:40,110 --> 01:38:42,780
So just forget
about it.

1190
01:38:44,380 --> 01:38:47,160
Don't you ever
say "never" to me.

1191
01:38:56,100 --> 01:38:58,910
Someone helped put a mirror
up in front of my face,

1192
01:38:58,970 --> 01:39:01,580
and I didn't like
what I saw one bit.

1193
01:39:01,640 --> 01:39:05,490
You know what I did?
I changed.

1194
01:39:05,540 --> 01:39:09,450
And that someone...
was Mrs. Threadgoode.

1195
01:39:09,510 --> 01:39:14,020
She needs my love
and care, and I'm
gonna give it to her.

1196
01:39:15,780 --> 01:39:19,420
If you'll excuse me,
I have to go to the gym.

1197
01:39:24,360 --> 01:39:27,400
And if you won't listen
to reason...

1198
01:39:27,460 --> 01:39:31,100
there's always Towanda.

1199
01:39:45,880 --> 01:39:48,860
Hey, Nin-

1200
01:39:51,520 --> 01:39:54,560
What are you doing?

1201
01:39:54,620 --> 01:39:57,360
Those are her things,
Mrs. Threadgoode's things!

1202
01:39:57,420 --> 01:40:00,530
- What are you doing in here?
Where's Mrs. Threadgoode?
- Who?

1203
01:40:00,590 --> 01:40:03,430
Mrs. Threadgoode!
The woman who lives here.
Are you deaf?

1204
01:40:03,500 --> 01:40:06,410
I'm sorry, miss.
All they told me...

1205
01:40:06,470 --> 01:40:10,680
was that the woman who lived
in here died this morning.

1206
01:40:12,540 --> 01:40:14,680
Oh. my God!

1207
01:40:14,740 --> 01:40:19,090
Wha- What
are you sayin'?

1208
01:40:19,150 --> 01:40:21,320
She died early
this morning.

1209
01:40:21,380 --> 01:40:25,730
They were shorthanded
so they asked me to take
all this stuff down.

1210
01:40:25,790 --> 01:40:28,290
That? all I know.

1211
01:40:47,670 --> 01:40:49,620
Stop that!

1212
01:40:49,680 --> 01:40:52,060
What is the matter
with you people?

1213
01:40:52,110 --> 01:40:55,060
Can't you wait a goddamn day,
for Chrissake?

1214
01:40:55,120 --> 01:40:58,120
Do you have no respect?
These are her things!

1215
01:40:58,190 --> 01:41:02,370
I'm sorry, but they told me
to get this room ready
for another patient.

1216
01:41:02,420 --> 01:41:05,630
She may be just
another patient to you,

1217
01:41:05,690 --> 01:41:09,800
- but she was my friend,
and I loved her.
- I'm sorry.

1218
01:41:09,860 --> 01:41:11,810
I'm just
following orders.

1219
01:41:11,870 --> 01:41:14,820
- What is going on?
- Why didn't
you call me?

1220
01:41:14,870 --> 01:41:18,220
- You could've called me before
you sent that idiot-
- I'm sorry.

1221
01:41:18,270 --> 01:41:20,940
It never occurred to me
that you would take it
this hard.

1222
01:41:21,010 --> 01:41:24,650
- I didn't even get
to tell her good-bye.
- Oh, I know.

1223
01:41:24,710 --> 01:41:28,680
These things are difficult,
but she died peacefully
in her sleep.

1224
01:41:28,750 --> 01:41:32,030
To tell you the truth,
I thought you'd be happy
for Mrs. Threadgoode.

1225
01:41:32,090 --> 01:41:35,130
- Happy?
- Why, yes!
This is what she wanted.

1226
01:41:35,190 --> 01:41:37,140
What?
To be dead?

1227
01:41:37,190 --> 01:41:39,730
No, to go home.
You just missed her.

1228
01:41:39,790 --> 01:41:42,240
She left in a yellow cab
about a half hour ago.

1229
01:41:42,300 --> 01:41:45,010
I don't understand.
What? A cab?

1230
01:41:45,070 --> 01:41:49,350
She said there wasn't no
reason for her to stay now
that Mrs. Otis had died.

1231
01:41:49,400 --> 01:41:52,040
Mrs...

1232
01:41:52,110 --> 01:41:54,280
Otis is dead?

1233
01:41:54,340 --> 01:41:58,220
Oh, Mrs. Otis died.

1234
01:41:58,280 --> 01:42:00,280
Mrs. Otis died!

1235
01:42:00,350 --> 01:42:03,560
Mrs. Otis!
Oh, God!

1236
01:42:03,620 --> 01:42:07,660
Not that... I'm glad that
Mrs. Otis died, it's just-

1237
01:42:07,720 --> 01:42:10,360
Oh, God.
I've gotta stop her.

1238
01:42:49,800 --> 01:42:53,040
Hey, Evelyn,
somebody stole my house.

1239
01:42:53,100 --> 01:42:56,010
It was right here
when I left.

1240
01:42:56,070 --> 01:43:00,850
Unless- Oh, Evelyn,
you don't reckon
I'm crazy, do you?

1241
01:43:00,910 --> 01:43:05,120
- It was here
when I left.
- No, honey,
you're not crazy.

1242
01:43:05,180 --> 01:43:07,960
This is the place.

1243
01:43:08,020 --> 01:43:12,060
Why would anyone want to
steal an old lady's home?

1244
01:43:12,120 --> 01:43:14,260
Wasn't worth nothin'.

1245
01:43:14,320 --> 01:43:17,730
Oh, honey,
nobody stole it.

1246
01:43:17,790 --> 01:43:21,670
They had to tear it down.
It was condemned.

1247
01:43:21,730 --> 01:43:23,870
I'm sorry.
I shoulda told you.

1248
01:43:23,930 --> 01:43:27,210
Well, somebody
shoulda told me.

1249
01:43:27,270 --> 01:43:32,120
- I'm old.
I'm not a child.
- I'm sorry.

1250
01:43:32,170 --> 01:43:35,520
My husband Cleo and I
lived in this house...

1251
01:43:35,580 --> 01:43:38,080
for more than 40 years.

1252
01:43:38,150 --> 01:43:41,560
Now, it's... it's gone.

1253
01:43:41,620 --> 01:43:45,190
83 years worth of livin'
and all that's left of me...

1254
01:43:45,250 --> 01:43:49,290
is what's in this box, a
bunch of old cards and pictures.

1255
01:43:49,360 --> 01:43:51,840
Come on.
I'll take you home.

1256
01:43:51,890 --> 01:43:54,030
This is my home!

1257
01:43:54,090 --> 01:43:56,090
And now it's gone.

1258
01:43:56,160 --> 01:43:58,700
And Mrs. Otis
is gone.

1259
01:43:58,770 --> 01:44:00,880
I...

1260
01:44:00,930 --> 01:44:03,540
I don't quite
know what to do.

1261
01:44:03,600 --> 01:44:07,450
This is the first time
I can remember when I don't
have a soul to look after.

1262
01:44:07,510 --> 01:44:09,890
You can come
look after me and Ed.

1263
01:44:09,940 --> 01:44:12,250
Oh, you're sweet,

1264
01:44:12,310 --> 01:44:15,120
but I think you're doin'
just fine on your own.

1265
01:44:15,180 --> 01:44:19,490
Don't you know you'd be
like a gift for us?

1266
01:44:19,550 --> 01:44:22,720
You're the reason
I get up every morning...

1267
01:44:22,790 --> 01:44:26,140
and that Mary Kay's
havin' such a good year...

1268
01:44:26,190 --> 01:44:30,760
and I don't look like some
blob from a horror movie.

1269
01:44:30,830 --> 01:44:34,870
Well,with a little help
from Idgie and Ruth.

1270
01:44:36,440 --> 01:44:38,980
Come on. I've got
your room all ready.

1271
01:44:39,040 --> 01:44:41,450
What does Ed say
about all this?

1272
01:44:41,510 --> 01:44:45,360
He'll learn
to love it.

1273
01:44:48,820 --> 01:44:52,960
Did I ever tell you
that Mrs. Otis was
Sipsey's baby sister?

1274
01:44:53,020 --> 01:44:55,690
- No, ma'am.
- Yes, she was.

1275
01:44:55,760 --> 01:44:59,640
Mrs. Otis was with
Sipsey and me the
night Sipsey died.

1276
01:45:17,930 --> 01:45:21,470
- Hey there!
- You got to come quick.

1277
01:45:21,530 --> 01:45:26,500
- The show has hardly begun.
- You got to come quick.
You hear me?

1278
01:45:32,410 --> 01:45:35,020
- Run, get help!
Run, quick!
- Where's the baby?

1279
01:45:35,080 --> 01:45:36,890
Never mind.

1280
01:45:55,600 --> 01:45:57,270
Excuse me, sir.

1281
01:45:57,330 --> 01:46:02,840
I don't believe you
should be goin' anywhere
with Ruth's baby.

1282
01:46:14,490 --> 01:46:17,230
Like I said,
you ain't goin' nowhere.

1283
01:46:17,290 --> 01:46:19,860
Damn, you a thickheaded
son-of-a-bitch, ain't you?

1284
01:46:24,060 --> 01:46:26,040
I told you...

1285
01:46:26,100 --> 01:46:30,550
you ain't goin' nowheres
with Miss Ruth's baby.

1286
01:46:36,170 --> 01:46:38,380
Come on, angel.
Come on.

1287
01:46:38,440 --> 01:46:42,290
Come on, sweetheart.
It's all right.

1288
01:46:42,350 --> 01:46:44,850
Come on.
It's all right, baby.

1289
01:46:47,750 --> 01:46:50,490
it was self-defense.

1290
01:46:50,550 --> 01:46:55,400
I don't know why any
white jury would care
why I did it.

1291
01:46:55,460 --> 01:46:58,270
- Well, I saw it,
and I can testify.
- Excuse me here.

1292
01:46:58,330 --> 01:47:00,500
I don't mean
no offense here,

1293
01:47:00,560 --> 01:47:03,630
but I don't know who's less
likely to convince a jury,

1294
01:47:03,700 --> 01:47:05,980
my mama...
or Mr. Smokey.

1295
01:47:06,040 --> 01:47:08,850
No offense taken.

1296
01:47:08,910 --> 01:47:11,320
You're a good man,
Mr. Smokey.

1297
01:47:11,380 --> 01:47:15,420
- You did good.
- The sun's almost up.

1298
01:47:18,950 --> 01:47:22,330
- George?
- Mm-hmm?

1299
01:47:22,390 --> 01:47:25,170
I think...

1300
01:47:25,220 --> 01:47:28,760
it's hog-boiling time.

1301
01:47:28,830 --> 01:47:31,110
No, ma'am. It
ain't cold enough.

1302
01:47:31,160 --> 01:47:33,940
It's hog-boiling time.

1303
01:47:36,870 --> 01:47:38,820
Big George?

1304
01:47:38,870 --> 01:47:41,980
- Uh-huh?
- When is that barbecue
gonna be ready?

1305
01:47:42,040 --> 01:47:44,380
It's gonna be ready
any time now.

1306
01:47:44,440 --> 01:47:49,360
Smells so damn good I just
can't wait to get me some.

1307
01:47:49,410 --> 01:47:53,720
- Now, don't you forget
to call me when that's ready.
- All right.

1308
01:48:07,460 --> 01:48:09,740
Here you go.

1309
01:48:11,300 --> 01:48:14,940
- Miss Idgie?
Smokey left town.
- Yeah?

1310
01:48:15,010 --> 01:48:19,020
I thought it'd be best
under the circumstances.

1311
01:48:19,080 --> 01:48:23,050
He asked that
you tell Ruth good-bye.

1312
01:48:23,110 --> 01:48:25,590
Shame he had to go.

1313
01:48:32,560 --> 01:48:37,480
Hold on! I'm comin'.

1314
01:48:42,330 --> 01:48:45,110
- What you want?
- We want some barbecue.

1315
01:48:45,170 --> 01:48:48,880
Not today you don't.
Go on.

1316
01:49:01,920 --> 01:49:05,060
Why, this is about the
best barbecue I ever ate!

1317
01:49:06,560 --> 01:49:10,060
The secret's
in the sauce.

1318
01:49:18,840 --> 01:49:22,720
Sipsey?
My God!

1319
01:49:28,230 --> 01:49:31,640
about what the most
important thing in life is.

1320
01:49:31,700 --> 01:49:34,040
- Do you know
what I think it is?
- No, ma'am.

1321
01:49:34,100 --> 01:49:37,380
Friends.
Best friends.

1322
01:49:37,440 --> 01:49:40,480
Oh. Ninny!

1323
01:49:41,640 --> 01:49:43,380
Look.

1324
01:49:48,650 --> 01:49:50,490
Oh!

1325
01:50:09,700 --> 01:50:11,650
Idgie?

1326
01:50:15,110 --> 01:50:18,990
- Idgie's alive?
- Oh, yes!

1327
01:50:19,050 --> 01:50:23,330
She's still out and about
Charmin' bees and selling honey.

1328
01:50:23,380 --> 01:50:27,350
Sometimes I think
I catch a glimpse of her.

1329
01:50:33,260 --> 01:50:35,710
Maybe we'll
see her today.

1330
01:50:35,760 --> 01:50:38,400
Maybe.

1331
01:50:40,070 --> 01:50:42,780
Let's go.

1332
01:50:54,280 --> 01:50:58,590
After Ruth died and
the railroad stopped runnin',

1333
01:50:58,650 --> 01:51:02,660
the cafe shut down, and everybody
just scattered to the winds.

1334
01:51:03,990 --> 01:51:07,370
It was never more than just
a little knockabout place.

1335
01:51:07,430 --> 01:51:10,240
But now that
I look back on it,

1336
01:51:10,300 --> 01:51:12,580
when that cafe closed...

1337
01:51:12,630 --> 01:51:16,740
the heart of the town
just stopped beating.

1338
01:51:16,800 --> 01:51:19,640
It's funny how
a little place like this...

1339
01:51:19,710 --> 01:51:23,560
brought so
